{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/47","id":4686689497,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABF1k02Q","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/47","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/47.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/47.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/47","number":47,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"2849: reviewed instanton obstruction; original target unresolved","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Outcome\nThe original KP-3.51 question remains **unsolved**. The package records the gap between reducible-only representation sets and the nondegeneracy or local Floer information required by the known instanton L-space argument.\n\n## Narrow mathematical source check\nThe exact printed Definition 5.3 and torus-knot clause of Corollary 5.4 in arXiv:2608.20551v1 are tested using slope-6 surgery on the trefoil. The distinction between unsquared and squared character systems matters. This is a version-specific mathematical diagnostic, not a broader criticism of the paper or its authors. The trefoil filling is itself a known instanton L-space and is not a counterexample to KP-3.51.\n\n## Review\nThe frozen mathematical artifact passed separate adversarial review without mandatory corrections. All 114 submitted and 100 independent controls passed, including independent cohomology checks of all six squared rank-one systems. The abstract quartic local model is not asserted to be realized by Chern-Simons theory or by a three-manifold.\n\nOne substantive attempt used. Actual author and reviewer model: gpt-6-astra, xhigh. No novelty, priority, or full solution is claimed.\n\nQueue disposition: **unsolved, 1/5**. The campaign's single queue writer will add the row update. This commit changes only this problem's attempt folder.\n\nNo merge or release is requested.","created_at":"2026-09-30T06:22:40Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T06:24:48Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/47/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/47/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/47/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/487327b2412c436ae69e8c52bf353a9a1fb7594e","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:dot/math-2849","ref":"dot/math-2849","sha":"487327b2412c436ae69e8c52bf353a9a1fb7594e","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https:/